<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy · unottr"
  description="How unottr handles meeting data, AI requests, website visits, and purchase information."
  eyebrow="Privacy policy"
  heading="Your meeting library stays on your computer."
  intro="This policy explains what the unottr desktop app keeps local, what can leave your device, and the limited information involved in visiting this site or buying a license."
>
  <h2>Meeting data</h2>
  <p>unottr stores recordings, transcripts, speaker identities, search data, saved threads, and exports on your computer. unottr does not operate a cloud account or automatically upload your meeting library.</p>

  <h2>Optional AI connections</h2>
  <p>AI features run only after you configure a connection and make a request. A localhost model server can keep inference on your computer. If you use an installed agent or hosted API, that provider may receive your question, selected transcript excerpts, and nearby context needed to answer it.</p>
  <p>unottr does not send audio, video, frames, or unrelated files to an AI provider. The provider you choose handles submitted text under its own privacy policy.</p>

  <h2>Website data</h2>
  <p>This website does not currently use advertising trackers or analytics cookies. The hosting provider may process basic request information such as IP address, browser details, and request time to deliver and secure the site.</p>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>A payment provider processes checkout and payment details. unottr does not receive or store full card numbers. The provider may share purchase details needed to issue a license, deliver updates, prevent fraud, and handle support.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>You control the files stored by the desktop app and can remove them through the app or your operating system. You can disconnect an AI provider at any time. Purchase records may be retained when tax, accounting, or fraud-prevention rules require it.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>This page will be updated when the product starts collecting information in a new way. The effective date above shows the latest revision.</p>
</LegalLayout>
